 @connor040606  Not just that, Taxes in Europe, especially in nations like The Netherlands are crazy high.
21% is the norm in The Netherlands, so a ~1000 Euro MSRP GPU will have ~300 Euro in Taxes bolted onto the price, meaning the higher the MSRP gets the worse the pricing will be in Europe, cause the high percentage will lead to much steaper climbing prices.

Cause a doubling from for example 500 Euro to 1000 Euro would in the US mean something like going from 520 Euro to 1040 Euro, but in The Netherlands that can easily be going from 600 Euro to 1200 Euro. The difference in price gets worse and worse the higher the MSRP gets.

