 @Revener666  Take a look at Hardware Unboxed video on 5700xt vs 2070S update video. In Control the 2070S wins by 93% at 1440p ultra with DLSS enabled. That’s far from pointless. Also with no DLSS the 2070S still wins overall at 1440p for their game suite.

Also let’s look at the feature set. Intel’s XeSS is scheduled to come out and will require DP4A. Unfortunately for 5700XT users that won’t be possible but not an issue for 2070S owners. FSR 2.0 is luckily a thing now because FSR 1.0 sucked at anything but 4K and even then was vastly inferior to DLSS. FSR 2.0 still won’t be as good but it looks usable at least. NVIDIA recently wrote an API to make it easier for developers to deploy DLSS/XeSS/FSR all at once called “streamline”. 

Finally it depends on your use case. I have a C9 OLED and at the time the only way to get VRR working was to have a Turing GPU. I sold my 1080Ti and switched over to a 2070S mainly for that reason. Got rid of it for a 3080 when it launched so I could utilize the 4K 120hz VRR of the display. No regrets, it all worked out well and at no point was the 5700XT a good option for me.

 @Revener666  The 2070S was $499 and the 5700XT was $399 – no need to distort reality to fit your narrative. The Hardware Unboxed video shows the 2070S still wins at 1440p by 7% overall. In the case of Control it was 14% faster in a like-for-like comparison but 93% faster with DLSS set to quality mode (108fps vs 65fps). Pretty sure any reasonable gamer would take a slight hit to motion clarity for double the performance or the ability to use RT in that game which is actually pretty cool.

Also let's not forget the black screen debacle for 5700 XT users that lasted well over a year and several driver updates to attempt to fix it. Many folks just gave up by either returning or selling the card to someone else or they were lucky and never experienced it. I personally wouldn't want to roll the dice on expensive hardware.

Edit: Oh yeah and DLSS is the best version of modern anti-aliasing. Really nice feature for those of us who hate jaggies.

